WEBVTT

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.054
Hi, my name is Omer Orman and this is Fuel,

00:00:03.094 --> 00:00:06.714
Cars and Pollution. Built for the HydraDB
Hackathon.

00:00:06.846 --> 00:00:09.378
It connects oil prices, gasoline prices,

00:00:09.518 --> 00:00:11.578
driving, electric car sales,

00:00:11.898 --> 00:00:13.338
and transportation emissions.

00:00:13.522 --> 00:00:15.061
You can explore those connections,

00:00:15.301 --> 00:00:16.561
replay the learning process,

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.041
and trace the numbers to

00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:21.862
their sources. HydraDB stores the
relationships and their changing

00:00:21.862 --> 00:00:23.297
strengths. Each year the

00:00:23.297 --> 00:00:25.617
system predicts fuel use and emissions,

00:00:25.977 --> 00:00:28.616
compares those predictions with reported
data, and updates

00:00:28.616 --> 00:00:32.616
its relationships. The next prediction uses
those updated relationships.

00:00:32.691 --> 00:00:33.281
The experiment

00:00:33.281 --> 00:00:36.160
compares this approach with a nearest
neighbor lookup,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.312
a frozen graph, and predicting no

00:00:38.312 --> 00:00:40.612
change. Across 18 holdout years,

00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:44.857
the graph's reported average error was 1.77,
compared

00:00:44.857 --> 00:00:50.283
with 2.84 for no change. But the result has
an important

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.131
limitation. Remove the pandemic

00:00:52.131 --> 00:00:54.681
years and the graph loses to all three
baselines.

00:00:54.681 --> 00:00:57.781
The uncertainty intervals also leave the
ranking

00:00:57.781 --> 00:01:01.321
unsettled. This public demo replays saved
results.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:04.089
Its scenario controls show how learned

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:06.700
relationships, not proven causes.

00:01:06.751 --> 00:01:10.574
The goal is a transparent research tool.
Explore the

00:01:10.574 --> 00:01:12.334
evidence, inspect the learning,

00:01:12.514 --> 00:01:15.594
and see exactly where the model succeeds or
fails.
